n section reports every claimed item changed. An absent claim releases only for a row never claimed through that lane; an unreadable claim, unreadable current copy, or claimed row with no current active or closed specification holds naming why. spec_at returns path, text and why, and lane_hold compares a lane's claim at its base with its current or closed copy at the requested revision, and staged_closes identifies index moves from active into any terminal home: docs/archive/work/complete, partial or cancelled, or the legacy docs/work equivalent.\"","+detail = \"bound_items reads each current Done-when item that only ticks or evidences a claim-time item as that claim-time item; digest binds the work-item id and those items as sha256:<16 hex>. covering reads verdict lines under review records and decision entries: only a valid single-kind Done-when verdict, or a combined sitting passing the sitting validator with its line in its own ## done-when section, covers with a DONE-WHEN outcome CLARITY, BLESSED or SUCCESSOR and the digest, as does an owner-confirmed or owner-overruled decision entry carrying that digest; an unseen entry or retired reviewed key does not. claim_copy returns absent when its readable revision has no claimed specification for the work item, which releases every hold and produces neither a mint nor a brief; it returns unreadable when the revision or listed copy cannot be read, and unreadable_reason makes that a named hold at dispatch, hand close and merge and a mint or brief refusal. _copy_at gives both claim and current reads found, absent, or unreadable forms. blessing_owed owes when a readable current specification differs from a readable claim and has no cover; deleting its Done-when section reports every claimed item changed. An absent claim releases only for a row never claimed through that lane; an unreadable claim, unreadable current copy, or claimed row with no current active or closed specification holds naming why. spec_at returns path, text and why, and lane_hold compares a lane's claim at its base with its current or closed copy at the requested revision, and staged_closes identifies index moves from active into any terminal home: docs/archive/work/complete, partial or cancelled, or the legacy docs/work equivalent.\""," rationale = \"The same changed checklist is consulted at dispatch, hand close, merge and adjudication. One digest and covering predicate keep readers from accepting different texts or treating a verdict about an earlier text as a release.\""," test_refs = \"TC-325, TC-326\""," status = \"Approved\""]},{"oldStart":3280,"oldLines":8,"newStart":3280,"newLines":8,"lines":[" sr_refs = [\"SR-232\"]"," title = \"Combined sitting composes and validates kind-scoped adjudications\""," module = \"project-trajectory/scripts/adjudicate_brief.py;project-trajectory/scripts/kitlib/sitting.py\"","-code_symbol = \"requested_kinds/_named_kinds/_sitting_scopes/combined_values/_sitting_refusal;scopes/sections/own_section/brief_scope\"","-detail = \"A combined class accepts only amendment:<id>, first-approval:<id> and done-when:<id> Adjudicates tokens; it composes each named class through compose with that section's verdict path in fixed amendment, first-approval, done-when order, and refuses whole if any section cannot compose. Its verdict is checked against the kinds requested by its composed brief: it refuses no requested kinds, a different SITTING: JUDGED kind list, or anything other than exactly one heading per requested kind; each section passes that class's grammar. Token and section parsing are shared by composition, validation, act scopes and merge-time minting; the class is routed and retainable through BRIEF_PROMPTS.\"","+code_symbol = \"requested_kinds/_sitting_scopes/combined_values/_sitting_refusal;scopes/sections/own_section/brief_scope/GRAMMAR/DONE_WHEN_OUTCOMES/line_refusal/named_kinds/sitting_refusal/kind_part\"","+detail = \"A combined class accepts only amendment:<id>, first-approval:<id> and done-when:<id> Adjudicates tokens; it composes each named class through compose with that section's verdict path in fixed amendment, first-approval, done-when order, and refuses whole if any section cannot compose. Its verdict is checked against the kinds requested by its composed brief: it refuses no requested kinds, a different SITTING: JUDGED kind list, or anything other than exactly one kind-form lower-case heading per requested kind and no other kind-form heading; each section passes that class's grammar. The Done-when holds use this same validator and accept a Done-when line only from a valid verdict and its own section. Token and section parsing are shared by composition, validation, act scopes and merge-time minting; the class is routed and retainable through BRIEF_PROMPTS.\""," rationale = \"A shared checkpoint reduces adjudication launches only if no constituent judgement loses its scope or grammar. One parser prevents composition, validation and later acts from interpreting the same sitting differently.\""," test_refs = \"TC-327\""," status = \"Approved\""]}]},{"filePath":"C:\\Projects\\ai-template.wt\\wi-841\\docs\\archive\\last_approved\\docs\\test\\test-cases.toml","hunks":[{"oldStart":3312,"oldLines":32,"newStart":3312,"newLines":32,"lines":[" [test.TC-326]"," verifies = [\"SR-156\", \"LLR-307\", \"LLR-309\", \"IF-286\"]"," level = \"Integration\"","-method = \"Run test_a_covering_verdict_releases_the_dispatch_and_the_close, test_an_owner_ruling_binding_the_digest_releases_and_an_unseen_one_does_not, test_a_confirmed_ruling_still_carrying_the_retired_reviewed_key_does_not_release, and test_changing_the_text_after_a_verdict_holds_again. Assert each covering verdict outcome and a seen matching owner ruling releases, an unseen or retired-key ruling does not, and a later text change owes a fresh blessing.\"","+method = \"Run test_a_covering_verdict_releases_the_dispatch_and_the_close, test_an_owner_ruling_binding_the_digest_releases_and_an_unse