{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfnKjMDF9vcFp8xuvUTq2","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"All six amended rows change meaning (`VERDICT: MEANING rows=6`). I'd bless each new text, so I re-attested all six.\n\nThe common thread: a sitting that fails validation now counts as no verdict at all.\n\n- **LLR-262:** a sitting with a missing or repeated done-when section, or a DONE-WHEN line under another heading, used to make the merge-time mint refuse. Now it covers nothing, and the merge mints the usual done-when adjudication row instead. Repeated Dispositions inside a valid section, or a SUCCESSOR part with no draft, still refuse.\n- **LLR-307:** a DONE-WHEN line used to count as a blessing wherever it appeared. Now only a valid single-kind verdict, or a combined sitting that passes validation with the line in its own `## done-when` section, releases a hold.\n- **LLR-310:** a combined verdict carrying any section that wasn't requested is now refused, and the Done-when holds use this same validator.\n- **TC-326, TC-327, TC-328:** each adds the matching cases and tests: a rejected sitting releases nothing, an unrequested section refuses the verdict, and a SUCCESSOR line outside its own section leads to a mint.\n\n**Why I'd bless them:**\n- The six texts state one rule that fails safe: an invalid sitting never releases a hold, and its change falls through to the normal adjudication mint.\n- The tests added in `c34e12b2` check exactly these cases.\n- Each test case's run list names the tests its assertions need.\n\n**Commits:**\n- `79b11038` — the verdict file `010-ADJUDICATE-ef02f2b.md`, with the trailer `WI: WI-841`.\n- `07666890` — the re-attestation: `intake.py snapshot --reattests` naming all six rows. It copied both the LLR and test-case registries into `docs/archive/last_approved` and recorded act seq 50 in the act ledger.\n\nThe snapshot wasn't refused, so nothing else in either registry has drifted. The pre-commit checks passed on both commits, and the working tree is clean."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":610,"cache_read_input_tokens":300722,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":610},"output_tokens":697,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2cffbbc6-0175-4e90-b9ab-7b165e0c0246","uuid":"f4e6feff-2a6b-4759-b24e-3de7110fa017","timestamp":"2026-10-07T05:27:54.717Z","request_id":"req_011CfnKjLrAPKJViHBxiBpe9"}
